title: 'github feed: per-room/channel event filtering for subscription notifications (agent-configurable)'
updated_at: "2026-09-25T00:23:39Z"
---
Event-type filtering for GitHub feed subscriptions should live in clawq (not just GitHub webhook config), be scoped per room/channel (destination), and be agent-configurable: a user should be able to tell clawq in the alerts channel itself ("stop sending me check_run events for amaroo") and the agent updates the subscription/route settings via a tool.

Current state:
- Per-subscription preference flags exist (on_open/on_close/on_comment/on_review/on_status/on_merge in github_pr_subscriptions.notification_preferences, via `clawq subscriptions add --on-*`), but there is no agent-facing tool to read or mutate them.
- Newer github_routes have filter_json (include_events/exclude_events) but no agent tooling either.
- Legacy compat: `clawq subscriptions` CLI works over routes but is admin-CLI-only.

Acceptance criteria:
1. A tool (e.g. github_feed_settings) lets an in-room agent list and update event-type filters for its room's GitHub subscriptions/routes.
2. Updates take effect immediately (no daemon restart) and are visible via existing list/show commands.
3. Per-destination scoping: settings apply to the room/channel that asks, not repo-global.
4. CI-style filtering should support terminal-state granularity (e.g. notify only on workflow/check failures) — see related workflow-level CI filtering idea.
5. Docs updated; error messages follow src/CLAUDE.md actionable-error rules.